                     NetHack 3.6.7 for Atari ST (GEM)
                     ================================

A build of NetHack 3.6.7 with the GEM tile interface backported from
the NetHack 5.0 Atari port, trimmed to run on a STOCK 4 MB machine.


Requirements
------------
    - Atari ST-class machine (ST, STE, Mega ST/STE, TT, or Falcon)
      with 4 MB of RAM.  A stock Mega ST 4 is enough.
    - GEM AES (TOS, MagiC, EmuTOS, or FreeMiNT/XaAES).
    - For tiles: 16-colour (or deeper) video.  A stock ST reaches
      16 colours only in ST-Low (320x200); TT/Falcon or an emulator's
      extended VDI give the roomy 640x480x16 the interface prefers.
      In ST-High monochrome the game runs in ASCII (or the 2-colour
      Atkinson-dithered NH2 tiles).

    Known to work: Hatari with EmuTOS 1.4 at 4 MB, VDI 640x480x16.


Installation
------------
Unzip NH367ST.ZIP on the Atari side -- not on the Linux/Windows host --
because some unzippers translate line endings inside the archive and
corrupt nhdat.

The archive expands into a self-contained game directory:

    nethack.prg     GEM application (stripped)
    nethack.tos     the same binary; the .tos name starts it in
                    console (VT52 text) mode instead of GEM
    nhdat           packed game data
    NetHack.cnf     default configuration
    GEM_RSC.RSC     GEM dialog resources
    NH2.IMG         monochrome tile sheet (Atkinson dithered)
    NH16.IMG        16-colour tile sheet
    NH32.IMG        32-colour tile sheet
    TITLE.IMG       splash image (colour)
    TITLE2.IMG      splash image (monochrome)
    RIP.IMG         tombstone image
    run-hatari.sh   Linux/macOS launcher (Hatari, 4 MB Mega ST)
    license, symbols, record, nethack.txt, README.txt
Level and save files are written into the game directory during play.

Double-click nethack.prg to start.  On Linux/macOS with Hatari
installed, ./run-hatari.sh launches it on an emulated 4 MB Mega ST.


Display
-------
Tiles are the default; press F2 during play to toggle ASCII.  To force
ASCII text mode, edit NetHack.cnf:

    OPTIONS=ascii_map

For a pure text-console game (no GEM at all), run nethack.tos.


Notes
-----
Save and bones files are not compatible with other NetHack versions.

